title: Opening
---
<<portrait PortraitHandler Erin blank>>
???: Did you turn it on?
???: Just a second . . .
???: We don’t have all day, we need to make use of every second we still have access to this place.
???: I know—Just give me a minute! This thing isn’t cooperating!
???: Do you want me to help?
???: Just make it work already!
???: Got it! Rolling in three . . . two . . .
???: . . . one!!!


<<portrait PortraitHandler Eva happy>>
Eva: HEY HEY HEY EVERYONE! Welcome back to ForEva+! 
Eva: Today we’re switching things up a little! 
Eva: As you all know—


<<portrait PortraitHandler Eva annoyed>>
Eva: Er, well, SHOULD know, if you’re a real subscriber not some rando clicking in from the trending page and all. . .


<<portrait PortraitHandler Eva happy>>
Eva: So! If you passed the quiz and do in-fact know your stuff, congrats! You’re a true fan! 
Eva: And for those of you who didn’t, well, I guess I can tell you the answer. 
Eva: As of today, we’re dangerously close to 10 MILLION SUBSCRIBERS! 
Eva: And to celebrate, I thought to myself, why not put something else in danger! 
Eva: Our lives! 


<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angry>>
Vika: You’ve gotta be kidding. . .
Vika: You dragged us all out here to kill us didn’t you! 
Vika: I always knew you were a crazy bitch but not THIS crazy!


<<portrait PortraitHandler Eva happy>>
Eva: That’s right Vika! 
Eva: Tonight, this crazy bitch has dragged you all out to spend 24-hours in the most haunted mansion in the world!


<<portrait PortraitHandler Yvette neutral>>
Yvette: Oh wow.


<<portrait PortraitHandler Eva happy>>
Eva: According to the locals, decades ago a series of mysterious deaths occurred in the mansion, and every time someone spends the night. . .
Eva: By sunrise, they’ve disappeared!
Eva: So, obviously, it’s been abandoned for years! Nobody inside, nobody outside! Untillll today! 


<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angryClosed>>
Vika: . . .
<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angry>>
Vika: Did you fall for some shitty reddit hoax again!? There’s no way that’s true. 
Vika: At least I know my life isn’t in danger anymore. . . 


<<portrait PortraitHandler Yvette happy>>
Yvette: I wouldn’t be so sure about that Vika. 
Yvette grabs a piece of paper out of her back pocket and shows it to the camera. 
Yvette: This is a newspaper from a decade ago, it says a girl named Ruby went missing  the day she moved in. 


<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angryClosed>>
Vika: Let me see that. . .
<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angry>>
Vika: THIS IS FROM TEN YEARS AGO!


<<portrait PortraitHandler Yvette neutral>>
Yvette: Yes that is what I said.
Yvette: Wait—do you not know what decade means?


<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angry>>
Vika: You just HAPPENED to have a handy-dandy DECADE-old newspaper up your ass?

<<portrait PortraitHandler Yvette happy>>
Yvette: I like to come prepared, did you not read the email Eva sent?


<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angry>>
Vika: Of course not! 
Vika: Why the hell are we communicating via email, we LIVE TOGETHER! 
Vika: Hey wait a minute. . . 
Vika: THIS IS A PRINTED SCREENSHOT!


<<portrait PortraitHandler Yvette annoyed>>
Yvette: Does it matter? It’s a real article. And before you ask, not AI either. 


Vika opens her mouth to yell before quickly shutting it. 


<<portrait PortraitHandler Eva happy>>
Eva: Oooh, so you’re telling me little Ruby could still be roaming around in this mansion? Maybe we’ll bump into her!

<<portrait PortraitHandler Vika angryClosed>>
Vika: If it was that easy to find her, she wouldn’t be missing for a decade now wouldn’t she?

